{"id":"a3f07ffd-50ff-45a7-9798-f88e2b42ba93","object":"chat.completion","created":1784804911,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    payload = case[\\\"payload\\\"]\\n    round_scores = payload[\\\"round_scores\\\"]\\n    round_targets = payload[\\\"round_targets\\\"]\\n    forced = payload[\\\"forced\\\"]\\n    if len(round_scores) != len(round_targets):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Mismatched round_scores and round_targets lengths\\\")\\n    if not round_scores:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"No rounds\\\")\\n    n_tokens = len(round_scores[0])\\n    for rs in round_scores:\\n        if len(rs) != n_tokens:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Inconsistent number of tokens per round\\\")\\n    active = set(range(n_tokens))\\n    forced_set = set(forced)\\n    for idx in forced_set:\\n        if idx < 0 or idx >= n_tokens:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Forced index out of bounds\\\")\\n    round_masks = []\\n    for i, target in enumerate(round_targets):\\n        if target > len(active):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Round {i} target {target} exceeds active tokens {len(active)}\\\")\\n        scores = round_scores[i]\\n        ranked = sorted(active, key=lambda idx: (-scores[idx], idx))\\n        mask_set = forced_set & active\\n        if len(mask_set) > target:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Round {i}: forced count {len(mask_set)} exceeds target {target}\\\")\\n        remaining = target - len(mask_set)\\n        for idx in ranked:\\n            if idx not in mask_set:\\n                if remaining <= 0:\\n                    break\\n                mask_set.add(idx)\\n                remaining -= 1\\n        if remaining != 0:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Round {i}: insufficient tokens to meet target\\\")\\n        mask = sorted(mask_set)\\n        round_masks.append(mask)\\n        active = set(mask)\\n    final_indices = sorted(active)\\n    return {\\\"round_masks\\\": round_masks, \\\"final_indices\\\": final_indices}\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing Python source for solve(case). The problem: iterative token compression. Given case payload: round_scores (list of lists per round, each list of scores for tokens), round_targets (list of ints: number of tokens to retain per round), forced (list of indices forced to be retained, presumably across all rounds). The goal: start with all token indices (0..len(scores_per_round? Actually round_scores is a list of rounds, each round has scores for all tokens? The example shows two rounds, each with 8 scores, so 8 tokens total. round_targets: [6,4] means first round select 6 tokens, second round select 4 tokens from those 6? Forced indices: e.g., [4] means index 4 must be retained in every round. Process: maintain set of active indices. At each round, sort active indices by descending score (given round_scores[round_idx][index]). Then keep forced indices (if any) plus fill to round_target from top scores, but must preserve original order in the retained mask? The description: \"Preserve original order in every retained mask\". That means the output mask should list indices in increasing original order. Also \"reject infeasible targets\" if round_target > len(active) or forced indices not in active? Also \"stable_order\" means we break ties by original index? \"All ranking and traversal ties use the source position or identifier specified above\". So when scores equal, use index order (lower index first) to break tie? Or \"descending score\" then for equal, by ascending index? Typically tie-breaking by index.\n\nOutput: per-round masks (list of list of indices) and final retained indices. The example not given but should be returned as dict with keys \"round_masks\" and \"final_indices\"? The problem says \"Return the per-round masks and the final retained indices.\" In the solve function, we need to produce something like {\"round_masks\": [[...], [...]], \"final_indices\": [...]}. Also need to validate fields: case must have \"round_scores\", \"round_targets\", \"forced\". Possibly also \"round_scores\" length matches \"round_targets\" length? And each round_scores list length consistent? Also forced indices must be within 0..n-1. Also each round_target <= len(active) (after previous round removal). Also forced indices must be present in active set.\n\nImplementation: \n- Extract round_scores, round_targets, forced from case[\"payload\"].\n- n_tokens = len(round_scores[0]) (assuming consistent)\n- active = set(range(n_tokens))\n- forced_set = set(forced)\n- Validate: forced indices all in [0,n-1] and all in active (initial). \n- For each round i in range(len(round_targets)):\n    - scores = round_scores[i]\n    - active_list = sorted(active) (to have stable order)\n    - Sort active_list by (-scores[idx], idx) to get ranking: descending score, then ascending index for tie.\n    - Then construct mask: start with forced indices that are in active (should be all). Then add from ranking (excluding already chosen) until we have round_targets[i] indices. But we need to preserve original order in the mask: so after selecting indices, sort them ascending to get mask. However, the ordering constraint: \"Preserve original order in every retained mask\". That means the output list for round i should be sorted in ascending index order. So we select based on score, then sort.\n    - Ensure round_targets[i] <= len(active). If not, raise ValueError.\n    - Ensure forced indices are included. If round_targets[i] < len(forced_set), raise ValueError (infeasible) because we cannot fit forced indices.\n    - After building mask, set active = set(mask) for next round.\n- After all rounds, final_indices = sorted(active).\n- Return dict with \"round_masks\" list of lists, \"final_indices\" list.\n- Also include \"case_id\" from case? The problem says \"Preserve every source identifier needed to audit the decision\". Possibly include case_id in output? But the spec says \"Return only JSON-serializable values with the exact named fields\". Not clear if we should add case_id. Probably just the required fields. The task says \"Return the per-round masks and the final retained indices.\" So output structure: {\"round_masks\": [...], \"final_indices\": [...]}. Also raise ValueError for infeasible.\n\nEdge cases: forced may be empty list. Also if round_targets[i] > len(active) -> infeasible. Also after including forced, if forced count > round_target -> infeasible.\n\nImplementation details: Use list comprehensions.\n\nWe need to write solve(case) that does this.\n\nJSON escaping: must produce a string for the Python source. The response is a JSON object with one key \"implementation\" whose value is a string containing the Python source. We need to escape newlines as \\n, backslashes, quotes.\n\nLet me write the Python source:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    payload = case[\"payload\"]\n    round_scores = payload[\"round_scores\"]\n    round_targets = payload[\"round_targets\"]\n    forced = payload[\"forced\"]\n    if len(round_scores) != len(round_targets):\n        raise ValueError(\"Mismatched round_scores and round_targets lengths\")\n    if not round_scores:\n        raise ValueError(\"No rounds\")\n    n_tokens = len(round_scores[0])\n    for rs in round_scores:\n        if len(rs) != n_tokens:\n            raise ValueError(\"Inconsistent number of tokens per round\")\n    active = set(range(n_tokens))\n    forced_set = set(forced)\n    for idx in forced_set:\n        if idx < 0 or idx >= n_tokens:\n            raise ValueError(\"Forced index out of bounds\")\n    round_masks = []\n    for i, target in enumerate(round_targets):\n        if target > len(active):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Round {i} target {target} exceeds active tokens {len(active)}\")\n        # build ranking\n        scores = round_scores[i]\n        ranked = sorted(active, key=lambda idx: (-scores[idx], idx))\n        mask_set = forced_set & active  # forced indices that are still active\n        # But forced_set should be subset of active initially; but after rounds, forced indices may have been removed? Actually forced must be retained in every round, so they remain in active always. So forced_set subset of active always if we preserve them.\n        if len(mask_set) > target:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Round {i}: forced count {len(mask_set)} exceeds target {target}\")\n        # add from ranked until target reached\n        remaining = target - len(mask_set)\n        for idx in ranked:\n            if idx not in mask_set:\n                if remaining <= 0:\n                    break\n                mask_set.add(idx)\n                remaining -= 1\n        if remaining != 0:\n            # should not happen if target <= len(active)-forced+? Actually if target > len(active) already caught, but after adding forced, if not enough others, impossible.\n            raise ValueError(f\"Round {i}: insufficient tokens to meet target\")\n        # convert to sorted list for original order\n        mask = sorted(mask_set)\n        round_masks.append(mask)\n        active = set(mask)\n    final_indices = sorted(active)\n    return {\"round_masks\": round_masks, \"final_indices\": final_indices}\n\nNeed to ensure we don't mutate case. We only read.\n\nNow produce JSON. The whole response must be exactly one JSON object with key \"implementation\". So I will create a string containing the above code, properly escaped. Use triple-quoted? No, need JSON string with escapes.\n\nLet me write the code as a string then JSON encode it. Since I'm generating response manually, I'll do escaping.\n\nI'll write the code without any comments to reduce length? But it's fine.\n\nI'll ensure no trailing spaces.\n\nNow produce the final JSON."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1152,"completion_tokens":2226,"total_tokens":